HST Office: closing Page Setup with XDialog::endExecute() (a macro or extension over UNO) crashed the office on
Windows, in Writer (.uno:PageDialog) and Sheets (.uno:PageFormatDialog).

Page Setup's page tab holds a nested notebook (Margins, Paper, Layout; hst-dlg-page-setup.patch). When the dialog's
builder is torn down, that notebook's page windows are disposed before the notebook, whose item list still points
at them. endExecute leaves the dialog alive through its UNO peer, so its pending layout idle ran
SystemWindow::ImplHandleLayoutTimerHdl -> TabControl::GetOptimalSize -> ImplCalculateRequisition ->
get_preferred_size on a disposed page: access violation (minidump of batch5 9a2e846 on HST4). The Cancel, OK,
Escape and title-bar close paths never left the dialog alive, so they did not crash.

TabControl now skips disposed pages when it measures and positions them.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-dialogs-writer.py page-setup; tests/runtime/check-dialogs-sheets.py page-setup
---
--- a/vcl/source/control/tabctrl.cxx
+++ b/vcl/source/control/tabctrl.cxx
@@ -720,7 +720,8 @@
 {
     // resize/position current TabPage
     ImplTabItem* pItem = ImplGetItem( GetCurPageId() );
-    if ( pItem && pItem->mpTabPage )
+    // HST: a page window of a .ui notebook can be disposed before the notebook (see ImplCalculateRequisition)
+    if ( pItem && pItem->mpTabPage && !pItem->mpTabPage->isDisposed() )
     {
         if (  GetStyle() & WB_NOBORDER )
         {
@@ -2138,7 +2139,11 @@
             pPage = item.mpTabPage;
         }
 
-        if (!pPage)
+        // HST: when a dialog's builder is torn down, the page windows of a notebook nested in a dialog page
+        // (Page Setup's Margins/Paper/Layout) are disposed before the notebook itself. If the dialog outlives
+        // that (XDialog::endExecute keeps its peer alive), its pending layout idle measured the dead pages and
+        // the office crashed.
+        if (!pPage || pPage->isDisposed())
             continue;
 
         Size aPageSize(VclContainer::getLayoutRequisition(*pPage));
